## License category

This is a custom reciprocal source and user-sovereignty license. Its deployment and
Kernel-neutrality conditions may make it incompatible with licenses that prohibit further
restrictions. It is not represented as an OSI-approved Open Source license, a Free Software
license, or compatible with the GNU GPL.

## Preamble

Neutron is a personal cloud computer assembled as software inside a canister. Its user should be
able to inspect source packages, choose private or public packages, compile a personal system in
the browser, install a modified system, and keep control without a maintainer, registry, provider,
or governance body having a veto.

Neutron also separates infrastructure from products. The Kernel supplies neutral security and
computing Capabilities. Applications supply products. Similarly Situated Applications should be
eligible for each Capability under materially equal, documented rules.

This License protects those freedoms through copyleft, Complete Corresponding Source,
installation information, direct downstream rights, user-sovereignty conditions, and
Kernel-neutrality conditions. The Preamble and License Category explain purpose and
classification; the numbered sections state the operative terms.

